replace('models.tex','A draft product can temporarily have no variants; the diagram\'s one-or-more variant rule describes a complete published product, and publication validation enforces it.','The zero-or-more variant multiplicity permits draft products; publication separately requires at least one active, valid variant.')
replace('models.tex','Refund status uses Requested, Pending, Succeeded, and Failed.', 'Shipment status uses Registered, InTransit, Delivered, DeliveryFailed, and ReturnedToSender. A temporary failed attempt remains InTransit while redelivery is possible. Permanent non-delivery requires verified evidence and an authorised UC12 closure; it cannot overwrite Delivered. The first-release policy refunds the full captured order amount, including delivery, for this closure. A parcel physically returned by the carrier is counted and inspected through UC10 using a unique shipment/receipt reference; only saleable units are posted back. Lost parcels produce no stock increase. This is separate from a customer\'s UC08 return of an already delivered order.\n\nRefund status uses Requested, Pending, Succeeded, and Failed.')
replace('requirements.tex','The system shall validate and store carrier events and expose delivery status without allowing older events to undo verified delivery.','The system shall validate and store carrier events, protect verified delivery from older events, and support authorised permanent non-delivery closure with independent refund and physical receipt controls.')
replace('requirements.tex','Delivery charge is refunded only for full pre-dispatch cancellation in the baseline policy.','Delivery charge is refunded for full pre-dispatch cancellation or permanent non-delivery closure under BR15; post-delivery item returns exclude it.')
replace('requirements.tex',r'BR14 & A staff role confers only its assigned permissions. Customers can read or change only their own resources; suppliers have no direct software access.\\',r'BR14 & A staff role confers only its assigned permissions. Customers can read or change only their own resources; suppliers have no direct software access.\\'+'\n'+r'BR15 & Permanent non-delivery closure requires verified carrier evidence and Customer Service authorisation while the order is Shipped. It schedules a full captured-amount refund, including delivery. Restocking requires a unique physical carrier-return receipt and saleability inspection; lost goods are not restocked. Temporary delivery attempts do not trigger closure.\\')
replace('analysis.tex','Reconcile delivery event & Shipping Provider & FR14','Reconcile delivery event & Shipping Provider, Customer Service & FR14')
replace('analysis.tex','A failed delivery leaves stock physically outside the warehouse; saleable stock is restored only after verified return receipt and inspection. FR14 and BR08, BR10, BR13 apply.','Temporary failed attempts allow redelivery. Customer Service may close permanent non-delivery only with verified evidence while the order is Shipped; the system records DeliveryFailed and schedules an independent full captured-amount refund including delivery. Stock remains physically outside the warehouse until a carrier return is actually received, counted, and inspected through UC10 with a unique receipt reference. Only saleable units are restored; a lost parcel produces no stock increase. This path does not use the delivered-order customer-return eligibility rule. FR14 and BR08, BR10, BR13, BR15 apply.')
replace('analysis.tex','arising from cancellation, accepted return, or late-payment compensation.','arising from cancellation, accepted return, permanent non-delivery closure, or late-payment compensation.')
